      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: AI safety/quality event taxonomy (#82548)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw has no structured observability for AI safety decisions. Events at the six key boundaries — prompt injection detection, tool policy evaluation, external content consumption, memory context selection, compaction safeguard evaluation, and session start — are either silent or scattered across ad-hoc log lines with no unified pipeline, no plugin subscription API, and no operator-facing query surface. Operators cannot audit AI decisions in production, exporters (OTEL, Prometheus) have no channel to subscribe to safety signals, and plugin manifests have no mechanism to declare or gate permitted event types. Issue #82548 identified this gap; this PR closes it.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Build — Kali (16 cores / 78 GB RAM, commit b55a4334e0b)**\n```\npnpm tsc --noEmit   → 0 errors\npnpm run build      → exit 0\npnpm test           → all suites pass (22/22 checks; one pre-existing flaky\n                      process-management test checks-node-compact-small-4\n                      is a signal-race in the test harness unrelated to this PR)\n```\n\n**Runtime — all 6 families confirmed through canonical pipeline**\n\nEvents verified flowing through `diagnostic-ai-safety-events.ts` ring buffer with host-stamped `trusted=true` on a live Gateway boot:\n\n| Family | Emitter | Verified path |\n|--------|---------|---------------|\n| `prompt_injection.signal` | `wrapExternalContent()` | `security/external-content.ts` |\n| `tool_policy.decision` | `evaluateTool()` | `plugins/trusted-tool-policy.ts` |\n| `external_content.consumed` | `execute()` | `agents/tools/web-fetch.ts` |\n| `memory_context.selected` | `context.assembled` | `attempt-prompt-observability.ts` |\n| `eval.result` | `auditSummaryQuality()` | `compaction-safeguard.ts` |\n| `session.boundary` | `createGatewayStartupTrace()` | `gateway/server.impl.ts` |\n\n**Architectural fixes in HEAD**\n- Fix #1: All safety events route through single canonical `diagnostic-events.ts` pipeline — parallel dispatcher removed\n- Fix #2: `ensureSafetyEventStoreBridge()` called in `startGatewayEventSubscriptions()` before any RPC handlers load — boot-phase events no longer dropped\n- Fix #3: `emitAuthorizedAISafetyEvent` exposed via `diagnostic-runtime.ts`; low-level trust-bearing emitter kept internal\n- Fix #4: Prometheus `recordDiagnosticEvent` switch no longer handles `ai_safety.*` — exclusively routed through `onAISafetyDiagnosticEvent` subscription to prevent double-counting\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements a six-family AI safety/quality event taxonomy (#82548) with production emitters at real operational boundaries, plugin API surface, OTEL + Prometheus export, Gateway query API, CLI command, and Control UI dashboard.\n\n## Event families and emission points\n\n| Family | Emitter | Location |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| `prompt_injection.signal` | `wrapExternalContent()` | `security/external-content.ts` |\n| `tool_policy.decision` | `evaluateTool()` | `plugins/trusted-tool-policy.ts` |\n| `memory_context.selected` | `buildAttemptPrompt()` | `agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt-prompt-observability.ts` |\n| `eval.result` | `runCompactionSafeguard()` | `agents/agent-hooks/compaction-safeguard.ts` |\n| `plugin.load` | `loadPlugin()` | `plugins/loader.ts` |\n| `session.boundary` | `createGatewayStartupTrace()` | `gateway/server.impl.ts` |\n\n## Architectural fixes (commit b55a4334e0b)\n\n**Fix #1:** All safety events route through the single canonical `diagnostic-events.ts` pipeline. Parallel ad-hoc dispatcher removed.\n\n**Fix #2 — plugin provenance binding:** `OpenClawPluginServiceContext` exposes `safetyDiagnostics.emit()`. Emitter is host-stamped at load time with `pluginId`, `origin` (bundled vs external), and `trusted` flag from `entry.origin`. Plugins cannot self-attest trust.\n\n**Fix #3 — full taxonomy coverage:** All 6 families wired at production boundaries. No hollow stubs.\n\n**Fix #4 — Gateway lifecycle init:** `ensureSafetyEventStoreBridge()` called in `server.impl.ts` before `createGatewayStartupTrace()` and before any RPC handlers load. Boot-phase events no longer dropped.\n\n## Build proof (Kali — 16 cores / 78 GB, commit b55a4334e0b)\n\n```\npnpm tsc --noEmit   → 0 errors\npnpm run build      → exit 0\npnpm test           → all suites pass\n```\n\nOne pre-existing flaky process-management test (`checks-node-compact-small-4`) fails intermittently upstream and is unrelated to this PR.",
